"fn\">Y</span>)</div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.denote_mergeHead","kind":"theorem","line":2740,"name":"Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.denote_mergeHead","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.lean#L2740-L2769"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.denote_skipThen\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">CommRing</span>.<span class=\"name\">Poly</span>.<span class=\"name\">denote_skipThen</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/Basic.html#Lean.Grind.Ring\">Ring</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span>]</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">ctx</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Context\">Context</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">X</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">hf</span> : <span class=\"fn\">∀ (<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a>), <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.denote\">denote</a> <span class=\"fn\">ctx</span> <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span>)</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.denote\">denote</a> <span class=\"fn\">ctx</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HAdd.hAdd\">+</a> <span class=\"fn\">X</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.denote\">denote</a> <span class=\"fn\">ctx</span> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.skipThen\">skipThen</a> <span class=\"fn\">n</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">f</span>)</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.denote\">denote</a> <span class=\"fn\">ctx</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HAdd.hAdd\">+</a> <span class=\"fn\">X</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.denote_skipThen","kind":"theorem","line":2728,"name":"Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.denote_skipThen","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.lean#L2728-L2738"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">noncomputable def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.mergeHintG\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">CommRing</span>.<span class=\"name\">Poly</span>.<span class=\"name\">mergeHintG</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">norm</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">addK</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">comb</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">hs</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`mergeHintG norm addK comb hs a b` adds `a` and `b` following the hints `hs`, one per monomial of\n`b`, in order. `mergeHint` and `mergeHintC` instantiate `norm`, `addK` and `comb` for rings\nwithout and with a characteristic. A hint `h = 2*n + c` places the head monomial `k*m` of `b`:\n- the first `n = h / 2` monomials of the remaining part of `a` are kept, since they are greater\n  than `m`;\n- if `c = h % 2` is `1`, the next monomial of `a` is `k₁*m`, and the two are added into\n  `norm (k₁ + k) * m`, which is dropped if its coefficient is zero;\n- if `c` is `0`, `k*m` is inserted before the next monomial of `a`.\n\nThe next hint continues after `m` in both `a` and `b`. When `b` reaches its constant, it is added\nwith `addK`. If the hints run out before the monomials of `b`, the rest is added with `comb`.\nWrong hints produce a wrong sum, and the certificate `p = a.mergeHint hs b` then fails to check.\n\nExample: in the order `x³ > x² > x`, with `a = 5*x³ + 2*x² + 7` and `b = 3*x² + 4*x + 1`,\n`hs = [3, 0]`:\n- `3 = 2*1 + 1` keeps `5*x³` and adds `3*x²` to `2*x²`, giving `5*x²`;\n- `0 = 2*0 + 0` inserts `4*x` before the constant `7`;\n- the constant `1` of `b` is added to `7`.\n\nThe sum is `5*x³ + 5*x² + 4*x + 8`. With `a = x² + 2*x` and `b = -x² + 1`, `hs = [1]` adds `-x²`\nto `x²`, drops the zero monomial, and the sum is `2*x + 1`.","docLink":"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.mergeHintG","kind":"def","line":2697,"name":"Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.mergeHintG","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.lean#L2697-L2726"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">noncomputable def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.skipThen\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">CommRing</span>.<span class=\"name\">Poly</span>.<span class=\"name\">skipThen</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`skipThen n a f` keeps the first `n` monomials of `a` and applies `f` to the rest.","docLink":"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.skipThen","kind":"def","line":2692,"name":"Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.skipThen","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.lean#L2692-L2695"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">noncomputable def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.mergeHead\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">CommRing</span>.<span class=\"name\">Poly</span>.<span class=\"name\">mergeHead</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">norm</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">m</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Mon\">Mon</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">cont</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly\">Poly</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`mergeHead norm c k m a cont` places the monomial `k*m` at the head of `a`, then continues with\n`cont` on the remaining part of `a`. If `c` is `true` and the head of `a` is `k₁*m`, the two are\nadded (with coefficient `norm (k₁ + k)`, dropped if zero), otherwise `k*m` is inserted.","docLink":"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.mergeHead","kind":"def","line":2679,"name":"Lean.Grind.CommRing.Poly.mergeHead","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.lean#L2679-L2690"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.html#Lean.Grind.CommRing.Expr.eq_of_toPolyC_eq_toExpr\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">CommRing</span>.<span class=\"name\">Expr</span>.<span class=\"name\">eq_of_toPolyC_eq_toExpr</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">c</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Pr